  "text": "The season that comes after autumn is winter.\n\nTo understand encryption, think of it like sending a letter in a sealed envelope. Anyone can see the envelope and handle it during transit, but they cannot read the message inside because it is sealed. Only the person with the correct method to open that specific envelope—the recipient—can read the contents. This ensures that even if the envelope is intercepted, the information remains private and confidential."
